    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (77.96) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27). **Kyle Tucker** remains our premier start against the vulnerable Lance McCullers Jr., benefiting from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.75 and a clean platoon environment. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** draws a high-value matchup against Adrian Houser; his elite score is driven by a 14% boost from Houser\u2019s pitching profile and a significant 10% uptick for hitting leadoff. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Gunnar Henderson** (73.50) also project as elite plays. **Gunnar Henderson** specifically benefits from a slow-delivery opponent in Eury P\u00e9rez, which\u2014given our organizational emphasis on SB scarcity\u2014provides the necessary window for him to exploit the basepaths.\n\nThe decision to bench **Nolan Schanuel** was the most difficult call of the day, as his 60.11 score narrowly missed the cutoff. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects well against Noah Schultz, the optimizer favored the structural versatility of **Brady House** (62.72) and the aggressive deployment of **Heliot Ramos** (61.01). **Heliot Ramos** earns his spot today primarily due to a massive, exploitable matchup against Matt Waldron, whose 7.05 xERA is the softest target on the board. We are also keeping a close eye on **Sam Antonacci** (59.16); despite a suboptimal #9 spot in the order, his elite xwOBA of 0.407 makes him a high-leverage value play against Walbert Ure\u00f1a. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, as our lineup relies on several \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Should **Drake Baldwin** or **Liam Hicks** drop down the order, their efficiency scores will likely regress, necessitating a quick pivot. Furthermore, while **Nasim Nunez** and **Brady House** are locked in as starters, both face a 50% SB suppression risk against Bailey Ober\u2019s hold-heavy game plan. Owners should monitor the official lineup cards closely; if **Gunnar Henderson** or **Jackson Merrill** are rested, we will lean on the bench depth provided by **Marcell Ozuna** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 categories.",
